  "statuteText": "5:10-b Notary Fee Account. –\n\nThere is established in the state treasury a separate account to be known as the notary fee account. All fees which are credited to this account shall be continually appropriated to the secretary of state. The account shall be used by the secretary of state to fulfill the duties established by RSA 455:17. Twenty-five dollars of every application fee for a commission as a notary public or justice of the peace under RSA 5:10 shall be credited to this account. The fund shall be nonlapsing, except that any balance remaining in the account over $100,000 at the end of a fiscal biennium shall lapse to the general fund."
